     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose looks too high.\n\n**The issue:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum recommended dose of metformin is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the maximum. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day total in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order so pharmacy can review it."
      }
     ],
